;; stdlib/v16/engine.prn -- V16 JS engine, SPIKE: a complete (small) JavaScript execution engine in
;; pure PARENA -- single-pass source->bytecode compiler + stack VM -- whose every allocation comes
;; from an Arena, and which compiles (via the C emitter + any wasm32 C compiler) to a freestanding
;; WebAssembly module. Founder real-time (2026-10-15): "spike out the v16 js execution engine it
;; must run in WASM totally parena powered all arenas". docs/V16_NORTHSTAR.md's Phases 3-5
;; (interpreter, GC strategy, stdlib slice) in one narrow vertical cut; lexer.prn/parser.prn (the
;; Phase 2 expression-only front end) are left untouched and tested -- this file has its own,
;; complete front end because a statement grammar needs keywords, multi-character operators and
;; comments, which that lexer deliberately does not have.
;;
;; MEMORY MODEL (the "all arenas" answer to NORTHSTAR's Phase 4 GC question, for this spike):
;;   - there is NO malloc, NO GC, NO free. Every byte the engine touches -- tokens, bytecode,
;;     constants, the value stack, strings produced at run time, arrays, objects, output text --
;;     is bump-allocated from the Arena the host passes to `v16-eval`.
;;   - a run is one region: the host resets/drops that arena when the script is done. This is the
;;     honest GC substitute: nothing is collected mid-run. A script that allocates without bound is
;;     stopped by the per-run ARENA BUDGET (a RangeError, charged before each string/array/object/
;;     closure allocation) long before the pool itself runs dry, so the host never traps on a
;;     hostile script; the budget is a parameter (`v16-eval-bounded`).
;;   - compile-time-only tables (name tables, break/continue patch lists, upvalue descriptors) live
;;     in the same arena in this version; splitting them into a scratch region is a follow-up.
;;
;; VALUE REPRESENTATION: no boxed values. A JS value is a (tag, payload) pair held in two parallel
;; scalar Vecs (an I32 tag Vec and an F64 payload Vec) so the value stack never allocates per push.
;; tag 0 undefined, 1 null, 2 bool (payload 0/1), 3 number, 4 string (payload = index into the
;; string table), 5 function (payload = closure id: function + captured upvalue cells), 6 builtin
;; (builtin id), 7 array / 8 object (index into the object table); 15 is the internal "global
;; never assigned" marker that turns a read into a ReferenceError.
;;
;; REAL, HONEST SCOPE (a spike -- see docs/V16_NORTHSTAR.md for the rest of the road):
;;   - numbers are IEEE doubles; strings are byte strings (no UTF-16 semantics, no Unicode escapes).
;;   - statements: var/let/const (let/const are block-scoped, var function-scoped), function
;;     declarations + expressions + arrows, return, if/else, while, do-while, for(;;), for-of (arrays,
;;     strings), for-in (object keys), switch (default must be last), break, continue, try/catch,
;;     throw, blocks. Optional semicolons.
;;   - expressions: literals, array/object literals, + - * / %, comparison, == != === !==, && ||,
;;     !, unary -/+, typeof, ?:, = += -= *= /= ++ -- on variables and members, calls, .prop, [index],
;;     obj.method(...), `new Error(...)` (builtin Error family only).
;;   - closures: real, with shared captured variables (Lua-style upvalues, arena-allocated cells).
;;   - builtins: console.log (+ error/warn/info/debug), Math.{floor,ceil,round,trunc,abs,sqrt,pow,
;;     max,min,sin,cos,log,exp,PI,E}, parseInt/parseFloat/Number/String/Boolean/isNaN,
;;     Object.keys, Array.isArray, JSON.stringify, Error/TypeError/RangeError/ReferenceError/
;;     SyntaxError; array push/pop/shift/join/length/indexOf/includes/slice/concat/reverse/sort/
;;     forEach/map/filter/reduce/some/every/find/findIndex; string length/charAt/charCodeAt/
;;     substring/slice/indexOf/includes/startsWith/split/trim/toUpperCase/toLowerCase/repeat.
;;   - NOT yet: `this`/prototypes/classes/user `new`, finally, getters/setters, generators, async/
;;     Promise, regex, template literals, destructuring/spread/default params, labelled
;;     statements, Date/Math.random, JSON.parse, Unicode, per-iteration `let` binding in for loops
;;     (closures in a loop share one variable, like `var`), hoisting of function declarations
;;     (declare before the first call EXECUTES; a call inside another function body is fine),
;;     a garbage collector.
;;   - hard limits per run, all reported as ordinary errors, never a hang or a host crash: an
;;     instruction budget, an arena byte budget, a 1024-frame call stack, 64 nested try blocks.
;;
;; VS0 quirks respected (all rediscovered, see STDLIB.md "v16/parser"): no `let` inside `do`, no
;; variadic `+`/`or`, no struct field literally named `v` (collides with the generated
;; constructor's local), loop-tail values of Unit calls need a trailing `unit`, the arguments of
;; a call are evaluated in unspecified order (so two `(fetch! m)` in one call would be a bug --
;; they are bound in a `let` first).

(module v16/engine)
(import string)
(import vec)
(export v16-eval v16-eval-limited v16-eval-bounded)

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; constants: token kinds, operator ids, keyword ids, opcodes (zero-arg fns, the stdlib convention)
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
